# The scripts the terminal gives a Unix shell as it starts (Horizon/Assets/terminal/shell) are read by bash, zsh and
# fish on Linux, a Mac, WSL and Git Bash, none of which take a carriage return at the end of a line. A Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf would put them there, so they're LF whatever the checkout
*.bash text eol=lf
*.zsh text eol=lf
*.fish text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Horizon/Assets/terminal/shell/zsh/.* text eol=lf
